message.content:
This is a CBP ruling on trailer-mounted electric fracking pump units. The key question is whether the unit is classified as a reciprocating positive displacement pump under 8413.50 or as a pump unit under 8413.60. A trailer-mounted unit with a quintuplex plunger pump driven by an electric motor is a reciprocating positive displacement pump for liquids, so heading 8413 applies. Subheading 8413.50 covers other reciprocating positive displacement pumps, and the 8413.50.00 statistical suffixes are 8413.50.0040 (hydraulic fluid power) and 8413.50.0080 (other). Because the unit is a fracking pump, I think the classification is 8413.50.0080. Subheading 8413.60 covers other rotary positive displacement pumps, so it does not fit.

Heading 8413 also includes pumps fitted with a measuring device, and the unit could be a pump with a motor mounted on a trailer. The pump plus motor is classified as a pump under 8413 in any case. I am fairly confident 8413.50.0080 is the right result.

{"hts_code": "8413.50.0080", "reason": "The trailer-mounted unit is essentially a motor-driven reciprocating positive displacement (quintuplex plunger) pump for liquids, classified in heading 8413 as an 'other reciprocating positive displacement pump' under 8413.50."}
